---
const objections = [
  {
    title: "Made-up numbers",
    answer:
      "Every number here was measured by our harness on the bench Mac and comes straight from its rows. Nothing is estimated. A missing number stays missing, and the Report gives its cause.",
  },
  {
    title: "Cherry-picked runs",
    answer:
      "All runs of a test come from one attempt. A test runs again only when it is short of valid runs, and the new attempt then replaces it whatever it shows.",
  },
  {
    title: "Compared to what",
    answer: "The Bare CLI is Claude Code alone in Ghostty, and it runs every test. It is the gray line on every chart and is never ranked.",
  },
  {
    title: "Settings were tweaked",
    answer:
      "Each app ran as its maker ships it. We set only what has to match across apps: Opus 5.5, high effort, full access in its worktree and no automatic model routing.",
  },
  {
    title: "A newer version is out",
    answer:
      "Each result names the version it measured and never mixes two builds of one app. Results older than 60 days will be marked stale. Any maker can ask for a re-run on a new release.",
  },
  {
    title: "Blamed for our bugs",
    answer:
      "When our harness fails, the app gets “not measured” and never a bad number. Cloudroom's speed tests and Capy's tokens are ours to fix.",
  },
  {
    title: "Rules changed mid-run",
    answer:
      "Two changes landed during this pass. On 10 November, tests that were short of runs began to get re-runs. On 12 November, tokens moved to a step of their own. Both are dated in the method's changelog.",
  },
  {
    title: "Only one Mac",
    answer:
      "These numbers hold for a Mac mini M4 with 16 GB. A faster Mac moves every app and can change the order, so the harness will be public for anyone to run on their own machine.",
  },
  {
    title: "Why measure a \u201chi\u201d",
    answer:
      "Every new thread starts with the same fixed request, whatever you type. The “hi” isolates that cost. The real-question test shows what happens with actual work.",
  },
];
---
<section id="fairness" class="section">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 class="section-title">Fairness</h2>
    <div class="grid">
      {objections.map((item) => (
        <div class="item">
          <h3>{item.title}</h3>
          <p>{item.answer}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 48px;
  }
  .item {
    padding-top: 20px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-hairline);
  }
  h3 {
    margin: 0 0 8px;
    font: 600 18px/26px var(--font-sans);
  }
  p {
    margin: 0;
    font: 400 16px/24px var(--font-sans);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 28px;
    }
  }
</style>
